<pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="Ic78730293ba2d8d6c27ee833d27c519b59c6b717" commit="211104939226c81a7cca204d635b6960764390cd" commit_message="CHROMIUM: drm: rockchip: If disabling DMC, do it before changing mode  dmc_notify() configures a VOP LINE_FLAG interrupt to fire when the last line of pixels has been displayed on screen based on the current vop-&gt;crtc.hwmode, and then synchronously waits for this interrupt.  During mode_set, the drm crtc helper first calls the vop_crtc_mode_set(), and only updates vop-&gt;crtc.hwmode after it returns.  However, it is vop_crtc_mode_set() that actually changes the pixel clock.  Thus, there is a short window in time where vop-&gt;crtc.hwmode does not match the actual hardware mode - it still has old mode parameters, but the vop is actually scanning out using a new mode and clock.  If we call dmc_notify() during this time, it may configure a LINE_FLAG interrupt that will never fire.   In fact, this is exactly what happens when we transition from a mode where vblank *was* long enough to do DMC, to a mode where DMC must be disabled.  Fix this by disabling DMC earlier in vop_crtc_mode_set(), before changing the pixel clock, to ensure vop-&gt;crtc.hwmode still accurately reflects the real hw mode.  Note that with old code, we ended up with a hang with:  - vop_crtc_mode_set() - rockchip_dmc_disable() - raw_notifier_call_chain() - notifier_call_chain() - rk3288_dmc_enable_notify() - rk3288_dmcfreq_target() - flush_work() - wait_for_completion()  ...and then that waits for:  - process_one_work() - rk3288_dmcfreq_work() - clk_set_rate() - clk_change_rate() - rk3288_dmcclk_set_rate() - rockchip_dmc_wait() - raw_notifier_call_chain() - notifier_call_chain() - dmc_notify() - wait_for_completion()  If we move the disable to the top of the function everything becomes reliable.  It's OK to leave the enable at the bottom of the function because that's not blocking.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:48332 TEST=No more hangs, no more printouts about timeouts.  Change-Id: Ic78730293ba2d8d6c27ee833d27c519b59c6b717 Signed-off-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/316660 Reviewed-by: Derek Basehore &lt;dbasehore@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="316660" owner_email="dianders@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/60/316660/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Id55deadf24837575925414e4df9240173d36873c" commit="c397f44c9b6425662fdc5b3efde1b33537cb0dea" commit_message="Fix staging flags in enterprise_policy_base.py  This CL updates the chrome flags used for the cros-auto and cros-dev DM Servers in staging, when specifying the cr-auto and cr-dev test environments, respectively.  BUG=None TEST=Run test_that &lt;IP&gt; policy_RestoreOnStartupURLs --args=' mode=single case=NotSet_NoTabs env=cr-auto username=exc1@crosprqa1.com password=[per valentine/]'  Change-Id: Id55deadf24837575925414e4df9240173d36873c Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/315164 Commit-Ready: Scott Cunningham &lt;scunningham@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Scott Cunningham &lt;scunningham@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: David Haddock &lt;dhaddock@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Minghua Zheng &lt;mzheng@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="3" gerrit_number="315164" owner_email="scunningham@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/64/315164/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="3"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Id7b4c96f9a9aac8c4865df360e71a9a7ad6519b6" commit="70dce5a2e031b9595658678842aebd4fe26a3d79" commit_message="video_VideoEncodeAccelerator: Disable the test case for 240x136 videos.  The quality test is currently failing on some platforms. We are working on a more accurate verification method (PSNR with block). Before the CL is merged, let's disable the test cases for 240x136 videos.  TEST=Run the test on peach_pit BUG=chromium:548109  Change-Id: Id7b4c96f9a9aac8c4865df360e71a9a7ad6519b6 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/314610 Commit-Ready: Owen Lin &lt;owenlin@chromium.org&gt; Commit-Ready: Wu-cheng Li &lt;wuchengli@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Wu-cheng Li &lt;wuchengli@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Wu-cheng Li &lt;wuchengli@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="314610" owner_email="owenlin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/10/314610/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2015.07" change_id="Ia40d86c8d4b14857fa8822677b3f7d393a35b677" commit="44f90f25beb09accf48d15e01da9692ace224a48" commit_message="Skylake: Add GPIO ACPI Apis.  GPIO ASL APIs to get GPIO Value. Need such APIs to read GPIO config settings. Example: Kunimitsu need to read AUDIO_DB GPIO to identify codec select.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:44481 BRANCH=none TEST=build and boot on Kunimitsu.  Change-Id: Ia40d86c8d4b14857fa8822677b3f7d393a35b677 Signed-off-by: Subrata Banik &lt;subrata.banik@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/316352 Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="316352" owner_email="subrata.banik@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/52/316352/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="If78166a37936c097981dbc110258947270f5ebf1" commit="1143f019f50729910214e93f7d08137f2dff713f" commit_message="[autotest] Fix provisioning via test_that  Provisioning currently assumes you are running in the lab environment with an AFE. It used to use the AFE to verify the right image is installed on the device. This logic is unnecessary as machine_install would have failed if it could not properly update the lab AFE anyways.  BUG=chromium:463228 TEST=test_that chromeos4-row10-rack11-host17.cros dummy_PassServer \ -i peppy-release/R49-7712.0.0  Change-Id: If78166a37936c097981dbc110258947270f5ebf1 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/316476 Commit-Ready: Simran Basi &lt;sbasi@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Simran Basi &lt;sbasi@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Simran Basi &lt;sbasi@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="316476" owner_email="sbasi@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/76/316476/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I9f39fd751482db836c186d5a2024521d73c8e9a7" commit="db03bc2c1a6e1b75e733ce5f98eecac220e6159c" commit_message="[autotest] Validate --board and --build with test_that :lab:.  A board and build are both required with `test_that :lab:`. This adds a check to enforce that with a useful error message.  BUG=chromium:418379 TEST=run test_that using all combinations of --board and --build  Change-Id: I9f39fd751482db836c186d5a2024521d73c8e9a7 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/316513 Commit-Ready: Richard Barnette &lt;jrbarnette@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Richard Barnette &lt;jrbarnette@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Fang Deng &lt;fdeng@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Aviv Keshet &lt;akeshet@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="316513" owner_email="jrbarnette@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/13/316513/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I4101cd52b24959f8eee90a43288acf2900cad261" commit="73e7b2dd9dc9c46b8da9fb8c02469a89afb8f1b1" commit_message="Uprev update_engine ebuilds to latest AOSP.  BUG=None TEST=trybots  Pulled 19 new changes from platform/system/update_engine:   542c19b Remove SystemState references from DeltaPerformer.   33e91e7 Fix certificate checker callback lifetime.   2b4268c Fix crash on shutdown when update in progress.   ab49446 Restrict update_engine SSL certs.   b15a0b8 Remove SystemState from post-install step.   706a5ab Remove SystemState dependency from HttpFetcher and InstallPlan.   c1c17b4 Report Enum metrics from CertificateChecker.   9138ef5 Remove unused includes.   5609277 Add bspatch as a dependency of update_engine deamon.   9c12346 Fix temporary directory path in Android.   22ad861 Delete DownloadActionDelegate::SetDownloadStatus() method.   5bdc61b Revert &quot;Conditionally set dbus group in init rc.&quot;   5029dbb Conditionally set dbus group in init rc.   09af881 Enable rich status reporting for binder interface   2ec4aab Verify operation source hash if present.   cd60dca Fix update_engine build for non-Brillo targets.   4218b7e Disable DBus dependent targets when &quot;dbus&quot; USE flag is not set.   9e1eda9 Add Binder service for update_engine   a259179 Move metrics time helpers to metrics_utils.  Pulled 21 new changes from chromiumos/platform2:   3985694 init: remove WP screw bypass for block_devmode   3e75a3b cryptohome: Set attestation database ownership.   b326ee2 libchromeos-ui: Add --enable-wayland-server flag.   1b528df libchromeos-ui: Add --enable-arc when USE=arc is set   a959c67 quipper: Include large test data files using a compile flag   50efa41 quipper: Don't check build_ids_size in PerfRecorderTest   9d1ae25 p2p: Reduce the size and increase the timeout of HttpServer.Basic.   665b8a6 buffet: Update buffet to match libweave changes   6e83a6a power: Write to bl_power when backlight reaches or leaves 0.   d16b14f libweave: Updated for directory change in libweave   cf6f3c8 cryptohome: Add more retries when attempting blob decrypt.   131e86b debugd: Remove GetRandomPerfOutput and GetRichPerfData dbus methods   0b574db cryptohome: Add some more error metrics   5cd3998 power: Add ReleaseAllDisplayWakeLocks method   17d9145 init: Use /etc/sysctl.d instead of sysctl.conf   cbbfe72 cryptohome: Add checksum to critical persistent files.   c6af4e7 login: Remove verbose logging for the login system.   67b31b5 cryptohome: Use owner_password when locking nvram   b9cd17b cryptohome: Add more trusted EK CAs.   bd5d140 power: Leverage new power supply types to determine dual role.   2799a18 quipper: Makefile dependency on generated protobuf code  Change-Id: I4101cd52b24959f8eee90a43288acf2900cad261 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/316526 Commit-Ready: Alex Deymo &lt;deymo@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Alex Deymo &lt;deymo@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Gilad Arnold &lt;garnold@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="316526" owner_email="deymo@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/26/316526/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="I2fdfa4543937e79f2537cf409334cea8eedb770b" commit="e2253c28a4116335fcb014b3de6b88e0d0da285f" commit_message="UPSTREAM: ARM: dts: rockchip: make sure edp_24m is associated to xin24m on veyron  The edp-24m clock has two possible sources: the 24MHz oscillator as well as an external 27MHz input. The power-on-default is the 27MHz clock which is not supplied on all Rockchip boards. While on all current boards and also all Veyron Chromebooks the bootloader seems to adapt the muxing to the internal source, this doesn't seem to be the case on headless veyron devices like brain and mickey making the edp-24m clock an orphan. On the hardware side the 27m input also is not connected at all.  With the upcoming deferral of orphan-clocks this results in the power- domain code deferring, as it cannot request the needed clock and if the synchronous reset is sucessfullat all in this case is also unknown.  So fix that by making sure, the edp-24m clock is muxed to the internal 24MHz oscillator at all times.  BUG=None TEST=/sys/kernel/debug/clk/clk_summary shows sclk_edp_24m correct now  Change-Id: I2fdfa4543937e79f2537cf409334cea8eedb770b Signed-off-by: Heiko Stuebner &lt;heiko.stuebner@collabora.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; (cherry picked from git.kernel.org mmind/linux-rockchip.git  linuxrockchip/v4.5-armsoc/dts32  commit ba5810ab0c84069a73b4cd30582c77568158635f) Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/316004 Reviewed-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="316004" owner_email="dianders@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/04/316004/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ia93be812f6aba5308e3685a7f1b59c0838e0e46f" commit="d405827064620c0936ad5caf18d9841796a67729" commit_message="Shorten HWTest phase timeouts to reflect expectations.  HWTest phases have gotten faster since the timeouts for those phases were first set.  This reduces the timeouts for CQ, PFQ, and Canary runs to 90 minutes.  Although the timeouts are the same, the values are separately configured:   * Canary and PFQ runs share a timeout, because they share the     'bvt' pool.   * CQ runs have a separate timeout, because they their own 'cq'     pool.  Queries against CIDB suggest that the selected times are sufficient for most cases, except in the most extreme loads in the lab.  BUG=chromium:404191 TEST=run unit tests  Change-Id: Ia93be812f6aba5308e3685a7f1b59c0838e0e46f Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/316525 Commit-Ready: Richard Barnette &lt;jrbarnette@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Richard Barnette &lt;jrbarnette@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Richard Barnette &lt;jrbarnette@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="316525" owner_email="jrbarnette@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/25/316525/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><lkgm version="7713.0.0-rc5"/></manifest>